A||||2||Pete||'85 Fiero problem
Z||000000||Pete||04-03-99||07:26 PM||||I can't get my Fiero to idle.  I have accessed the idle speed screw.  When I adjust it, it only stays for awhile, then it begins to miss and stalls.  Could this be in the EMC box?  Thanks  Pete<br>
Z||000001||theogre||04-04-99||12:06 AM||||I'll asume you checked for vac leaks, including checking the EGR.<p>if it runs at other pedal positions, but won't idle, it could be the TPS, IAC, or the ECM. Which motor you have... the rest of this asumes a 4 cyl from you description.<p>The ECM uses the IAC motor to adjust idle air flow. It calculates this, if I have everything right, on 2 diferent sets of conditions. (this is the short form)<p>1. the engine is cold. The IAC is set based soly on PROM presets, and TPS "zero". TPS "zero" is the position the throtle is at when the key is turned on.<p>2. the engine is warm. The IAC is adjusted on the above, plus the input from the O2 sensor.<p>Check the ECM for codes. Check the TPS, replace it if it even looks worn. (it's 14-15 years old if it's the original. far older than it was designed for.) Check the IAC, replace it if need be. (IAC is a bit ecpensive.)
Z||000002||PaUL||04-07-99||06:16 PM||||I suspect you have a cracked EGR flex pipe. This part is notorious for cracking and causing a vacuum leak.
